# Cloudflare Pages redirects for wifiodds.com.
#
# Nothing needed yet: every route is a REAL file on disk (/index.html,
# /united/index.html, /alaska/index.html, /united/history/index.html,
# /privacy.html), so Pages serves them directly and there is deliberately NO
# SPA fallback ( /*  /index.html  200 ) — a fallback here would turn genuine
# 404s into a silent copy of the home page, which is exactly the "green light
# that wasn't looking" failure we avoid.
#
# Cloudflare Pages does NOT support Netlify's `!` force syntax or 200-proxying
# to an external origin; keep both out of this file (that combination broke
# every deep link on points-compass once).
#
# Placeholder for the smithfamai.com cutover era — add here if the old paths
# ever need to live on this side of the fence:
# /unitedstarlink      /united/   301
# /unitedstarlink/*     /united/:splat  301

# ── 28 Jul 2026 three-page cut ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every route below was removed from build/routes.js and its file deleted; these
# send the old URLs (and anything Google/inbound links still hold) to the home
# page with a real 301. Destinations are all "/", so order does not matter.
#
# The /united/ paths are enumerated EXACTLY, never globbed as /united/*, because
# united/data.json lives in that directory and the Chrome extension fetches it.
# A real static asset would win over a redirect on Cloudflare Pages anyway, but
# not writing the glob is the belt to that suspenders. Likewise /api/docs/ is
# exact so it cannot shadow the /api/* Pages Functions.
/airlines/            /   301
/airlines/*           /   301
/race/                /   301
/race/*               /   301
/systems/             /   301
/systems/*            /   301
/united/              /   301
/united/fleet/        /   301
/united/history/      /   301
/alaska/              /   301
/alaska/*             /   301
/roadmap/             /   301
/record/              /   301
/api/docs/            /   301
